  - question: Why did my gout flare when I started allopurinol?
    answer: >-
      When urate levels start to fall, crystals can move and cause a flare.
      This is common in the first few months. Your doctor may give you a low
      dose of colchicine to prevent flares while you start treatment. Do not
      stop taking allopurinol.
